From 89d016f17af2c172096e73a892625993b24123ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 05:22:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/25] sglang DSA: fix the PD+DPA+MTP draft-CUDA-graph
 deadlock

Adds eagle_worker_v2_uniform_draft_graph.diff, the fourth and final patch needed
for PD disaggregation with DP-attention and EAGLE MTP. With it the draft CUDA
graph can stay ENABLED; the previous 640/640 result in this file was measured
with that graph disabled as a workaround.

The graph/eager choice in draft() was made independently per DP rank from
rank-dependent inputs. Graph replay and the eager multi-step loop do not issue
the same host-side collective sequence, so the moment one rank chose differently
the group desynchronized and deadlocked on the first routed request.

Measured, not argued: instrumenting all four guard terms per rank per iteration,
the decision diverged on exactly the iteration that froze -- one busy rank eager,
seven idle ranks graph -- and that rank is exactly the one py-spy caught in the
eager init_forward_metadata. Reproduced twice with different victim ranks.

This also explains, for the first time, why single-node mix never hangs: on the
PD decode leg dsa_topk_indices is seeded from RDMA-shipped per-request payloads
(eagle_disaggregation.py:54-59), so it depends on which requests a rank holds;
mix seeds it locally, identically on every rank.

Fix: vote the local need-for-eager across the full TP group via a 1-element gloo
all-reduce on cpu_group (no GPU sync), and have every rank act on the group
answer. Must be get_tp_group(), not get_attention_tp_group() -- the latter is one
rank wide under DPA8, which would make the patch silently inert.

Verified 2540/2540 requests (PD conc 1->256, mix regression, 8-round durability)
against 0/4 for a same-node control with only this diff reverted. Over 2992
iterations the acted-on decision diverged 0 times while the local decision still
diverged 38 times -- the defect is latent, not masked by timing -- and the draft
graph is used on 98.4% of iterations, so the speedup is kept.

Also corrects two now-stale caveats in this README:
- the draft-graph limitation is closed by this patch;
- the "~2% degenerate output under concurrency" claim is WITHDRAWN. It was a
  test-harness error: the harness skipped GLM-5.2's chat template and forced
  temperature=0 over the model's own 1.0/0.95. With the template and correct
  sampling, 0/128 degenerate on both MXFP4 and FP8; the official FP8 build
  reproduced the "failure" under the wrong config identically.

Documents what was not validated: no performance comparison against the DPA-only
baseline, custom all-reduce still disabled, single context length and image.
